  :adr/context
  "ADR-2608170200 measured the JVM surface across 4,163 registered checkouts.
ADR-2608170300 built the gate that says whether a ClojureScript runner covers the
suite it sits in. ADR-2608170400 turned '2,034 repos have portable tests and no
runner' into a cost model and named the first tranche: 712 CLEAN, of which 322
needed no classpath beyond their own source.

This records what the tranches actually landed, and — more usefully — what they
did NOT touch, because the headline number is easy to misread as progress on the
JVM debt and it is not."

  :adr/decision
  "Two tranches, both verified before landing and both driven by tooling that is
  landed rather than hand-rolled:

  **Runner tranche** — generate `test/run_portable.cljs` for CLEAN self-contained
  repos, run it on the DEFAULT-BRANCH tree, land only what passes.
  `scripts/list-portable-runner-candidates.cljs` ->
  `scripts/sweep-portable-runners.cljs` -> `scripts/land-portable-runners.cljs`.

  **bb.edn tranche** — convert `:sci-test` bb.edn repos to an nbb test script
  (ADR-2607173000 retired babashka as the script host), again verified on the
  default-branch tree. `scripts/measure-bb-to-nbb-yield.cljs` ->
  `scripts/land-bb-to-nbb.cljs`, which drives the existing
  `scripts/bb_to_nbb_scaffold.cljs` against a WORKTREE rather than the shared
  checkout.

  **Pins move in batches.** `scripts/west-pin-put-batch.cljs` amortises the read
  and the write of a 1 MB west.yml over N entries while keeping the per-entry
  verification. It is landed because its write path was measured, not because it
  looked right."

  :adr/body
  "## What landed

| tranche | repos | tests now running under ClojureScript | FAIL |
|---|---|---|---|
| runner (`test/run_portable.cljs`) | **260** | 2,522 tests / 19,453 assertions | 0 |
| bb.edn -> nbb | **177** | 890 tests / 15,159 assertions | 0 |
| **total** | **437** | **3,412 tests / 34,612 assertions** | **0** |

Plus, by hand earlier the same day: 5 runner repos, `kotoba-lang/nekko` (all 17 of
its namespaces, 10 on nbb + 3 self-running + 4 compiled), and 2 cloud-itonami
actors.

Every one of the 437 was verified by running its generated artifact on the
default-branch tree and requiring 0 failures. 265 of 265 runner PASS rows and 178
of 178 bb PASS rows were processed; the 5 + 1 SKIPs are the idempotence check
firing on repos landed by hand earlier.

## Yields, measured rather than projected

    runner tranche   265 PASS of 322 candidates   82%
    bb.edn tranche   178 PASS of 181 candidates   98%

The bb yield is higher because `:sci-test` is a much stronger precondition: the
bb.edn had to already be a single `run-tests` scaffold. The 3 that failed name
their own reason — `System/getProperty` twice and `cljs.core/ExceptionInfo` once,
all three in the token classes ADR-2608170400 counts.

## The batched pin, and why it needed proving

Per-entry pin advance GETs and PUTs a 1 MB west.yml every time. Measured during
the runner tranche the landing rate fell from 12s to ~38s per repo as concurrent
sessions wrote west.yml and 409 retries piled up; ~200 pins that way is two hours
of round trips.

`west-pin-put-batch.cljs` makes it one round trip and keeps every check:

  - each entry is verified against the server (reachable from the default branch,
    `ahead` with `behind_by 0`)
  - ONE blob-SHA precondition for the whole write, so a concurrent writer gets a
    409 and it retries from a fresh read rather than forcing
  - one entry failing verification drops that entry, never the check
  - nothing is written if no entry survives

Measured on the real queue, both directions:

    102 of 102 entr(ies) verified -> committed d37ae9f
      manifest/west.yml | 102 insertions, 102 deletions
      added lines that are not `revision:` -- 0

    75 of 177 verified -> committed c669c71
      the other 102 dropped as already-at-that-pin

So the write moves exactly the revision lines it claims to, and re-running is a
no-op. The refusal paths were checked separately: already-at-that-pin, a sha not
reachable from main (404 from compare), and an entry absent from the tip.

## A defect I reported before measuring it

While reading the bb converter's output I noticed it can put `'clojure.test`
itself in the `run-tests` list, and wrote that it might therefore be in all 178
landed conversions. It is not: checked across all 177 landed `package.json` files
on their default branches, **0** contain it. The shape came from `ooyake`, which is
one of the 3 repos that failed to convert and was never landed. The flag was
right; the extrapolation was not, and the fix is to measure before saying how far
something spread.

## What this does NOT change

The original question was where this workspace depends on the JVM. Re-measured
after both tranches:

| class | repos | change today |
|---|---|---|
| `.clj` sources — the JVM is the runtime | **954** | **none** |
| third-party JVM jar in top-level `:deps` | **149** | **none** |
| JVM build toolchain | 292 | none |
| `bb.edn` | **363** in the detector | 177 retired ON MAIN; see below |
| fleet gates on `:jvm-test` | 66 | 3 flipped by me, 13 added by other sessions |

**Not one of the 954 `.clj` source repos or the 149 third-party-jar repos was
touched.** What moved is the TEST tier: 437 repos whose portable suites ran only
on the JVM now also run under ClojureScript, which is where a cljs-half defect in
a `.cljc` becomes visible. That is a precondition for the JVM exit, not the exit.

Also unchanged: the gate and the detectors read local checkouts, so none of this
appears in their numbers until `west update` syncs them. The bb.edn row above is
the honest form of that: the detector still counts 363 because the checkouts still
hold the file, while on the default branches it is gone — spot-checked on three
landed repos after fetching, `bb.edn` absent and `nbb.edn` present at the merge
sha. Reading the same three BEFORE fetching reported `bb.edn` still present, which
is the third time today a stale remote-tracking ref gave a confident wrong answer.
Recorded rather than worked around."

  :adr/consequences
  "- 437 repositories gained a ClojureScript test tier, 3,412 tests / 34,612
  assertions, with zero landing failures and zero forced pins.
- Six scripts land as the reusable path: three for the runner tranche, two for the
  bb tranche, and the batched pin. The next tranche starts from tools, not from a
  transcript.
- 186 bb.edn files remain, of which the classifier calls 167 `:complex` — those
  need hand ports, and `emit-batch` should not be pointed at them.
- The remaining runner work is named: 390 CLEAN-but-not-self-contained repos need a
  classpath from `clojure -Spath`, 1,134 MIDDLE are unknown until run, 169 FLOOR
  are definitely not portable, and 14 repos fail under ClojureScript for real
  (`mst` 262 errors, `glyph` 49, `katex` 37, `arxiv` 14).
- The JVM debt proper — 954 `.clj`-source repos and 149 third-party jars — is
  untouched and remains the actual subject of ADR-2608170200."

